  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 38039b016c60f49ef856ef184eaeb59e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Nopperabo_Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueData
  enemyDisplayName: "Nopperab\u014D"
  initialDialogue: You came closer than the others. Most run before I turn my head.
    A merchant last moon. A little girl two nights ago, no older than five, who called
    for her grandmother as she fled. They scream when I turn. They call me a thing,
    a haunting, a face that was not a face. So tell me, traveler. What do you see
    standing here? A person? Or only what is missing?
  options:
  - choiceText: '[I SEE YOU]'
    responseText: You looked. You did not look away. No one has said those words
      to me since the lantern-maker's wife. I had a name once. I had hands she would
      warm in the winter. Take this peace with you, traveler. The slope is quieter
      now.
    isCorrect: 1
  - choiceText: '[WHAT ARE YOU]'
    responseText: A thing. So that is all I am. Then I will be the thing you fear.
      Run, traveler. Run until your throat tears. The next face you see will be mine.
    isCorrect: 0
  - choiceText: '[LEAVE]'
    responseText: Yes. Walk away. Like the merchant. Like the child who called for
      her grandmother. Like every soft footstep before yours. I will weep here a
      while longer. And when you reach the soba stall at the bottom of the hill,
      do not ask the vendor about his face.
    isCorrect: 0
